  {
   "text": "I could not build the print-in-place hinge. The geometry engine rejected every version that joined the hinge knuckles to the box and lid, with intersecting faces, so no complete box with a working hinge exists yet.\n\nThree test pieces from my attempts are now on the plate: a 60 x 40 x 20 mm body shell, a 60 x 40 x 12 mm lid with its inner lip, and a 60 x 42 x 12 mm lid with one hinge knuckle. None of them is a finished part, so please delete them in Model before slicing.\n\nTwo ways forward:\n1. A 60 x 40 x 30 mm box with a friction-fit lid and no hinge. I can build this in one pass and it will print reliably in PETG.\n2. A two-part hinge with a separate pin, printed as loose pieces to assemble. This is less clean, but it avoids the fused-knuckle problem.\n\nNothing has been sliced or sent to a printer. Which option do you want?"
  }
